{
  "_comment": [
    "sg13g2-bandgap -- `klt sim` request template for closed-loop-zout-pex",
    "(issue #278). Instantiated by run_klt_sim.sh per (process, supply)",
    "variant, exactly like the vref bench; the seed set is per-supply, so",
    "the supply axis lives in per-supply body variants (an `alter`-driven",
    "supply axis would clobber the AC stimulus -- verified on ngspice 46).",
    "15 requests of 3 temperatures each, merged deterministically before",
    "the adapter.",
    "",
    "The declared analysis is the AC sweep; the bench body's own `.control`",
    "block runs the seeded `op`, the op prints and the same AC sweep (see",
    "the body's header for why), so klt's re-run of the declared analysis",
    "re-solves an identically-seeded operating point and the top-level",
    "`.meas ac` cards below attach to it.",
    "",
    "The four request-level measurements are LINEAR magnitudes, vm(vref):",
    "`v(vref)` in a `.meas ac` is the signed REAL part, which flips sign",
    "wherever the response's phase passes 180 deg (observed on the 3.63 V",
    "hot corners of the first grid run), while vm() is the magnitude. A",
    "resident-vector `.save` list disables `par('...')` in `.meas find`",
    "(ngspice 46), so the dB conversions happen in the enrichment pass",
    "over single reported values -- a unit conversion, not a differencing,",
    "so the 6-s.f. disposition is not spent. The op-point columns and the",
    "worst-case/frequency columns come from the per-corner log (body-side",
    "prints)."
  ],
  "engine": "ngspice",
  "netlist": "@@BODY@@",
  "netlist_source": "extracted",
  "models": {
    "lib": "@@CORNER_BUNDLE@@"
  },
  "corners": {
    "process": [
      "typ",
      "bcs",
      "wcs",
      "sf",
      "fs"
    ],
    "temperature_c": [
      -40,
      27,
      125
    ]
  },
  "analysis": {
    "kind": "ac",
    "args": "dec 30 1 1e9"
  },
  "measurements": [
    {
      "name": "zout_dc_lin",
      "spice": ".meas ac zout_dc_lin find vm(vref) at=1"
    },
    {
      "name": "zout_1khz_lin",
      "spice": ".meas ac zout_1khz_lin find vm(vref) at=1k"
    },
    {
      "name": "zout_100khz_lin",
      "spice": ".meas ac zout_100khz_lin find vm(vref) at=100k"
    },
    {
      "name": "zout_1mhz_lin",
      "spice": ".meas ac zout_1mhz_lin find vm(vref) at=1meg"
    }
  ],
  "options": {
    "timeout_s": 900,
    "keep_artifacts": true
  }
}
